// The negative half of the masking rule: `!` on a fixed-width integer yields *that* width, not
// `int`. Without this the value could be masked correctly and still leak into an `int` position,
// where the next operation would wrap at 64 bits instead. E0007 names the width the complement kept.
// expect: error E0007 at 7:10
// expect: exit 1
x: u8 = 1;
y: int = !x;
echo y;
